--000000000000dd28e605a926da02
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="UTF-8"

I don't see a problem with adding this extra place as what people already
know is still valid and this last place would just be elided. This is an
enhancement only and can be easily explained on the fly. If it comes up
only one or two times I believe most speakers will remember it. I'm not
saying there isn't now a way to say, for instance, that you are playing
chess. This is a more straightforward way to do it, though.

Adding to the end of a gismu is much less of a change than changing it in
the middle. When we were originally working on place structures for the
gismu long ago we knew there would be some that needed to be expanded (and
shortened).

. karis. /Karen Stein


